⭐ What is happening?
Asynchronous
producer.send(record, callback);

Means:

Send the message and don't wait for the result immediately.

The callback tells us whether the message was successfully sent.

Synchronous
producer.send(record).get();

Means:

Send the message and wait for the result before continuing.

🧠 Easy difference for viva
Asynchronous	Synchronous
Does not wait	Waits for response
Faster	Comparatively slower
Uses callback	Uses get()
Multiple sends can proceed	Each send waits
Example: send(record, callback)	Example: send(record).get()
One-line viva answer:

Asynchronous sending sends the message without waiting for the result, whereas synchronous sending waits for the broker acknowledgement before continuing.

